    {
      "external_key": "alg2-quadratic-formula-irrational",
      "topic": "Quadratic Functions",
      "subtopic": "Quadratic formula",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["quadratics", "quadratic-formula", "radicals"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "4",
      "source_section": "4.6",
      "statement": "Solve using the quadratic formula. Leave your answer in exact form.\n$$ {{coef(a,'x^2')}} {{term(b,'x')}} {{signed(c)}} = 0 $$",
      "answer": "$x = \\dfrac{ {{-b}} \\pm {{radical(disc)}} }{ {{2*a}} }$",
      "solution": "Here $a = {{a}}$, $b = {{b}}$, $c = {{c}}$, so the discriminant is $b^2 - 4ac = {{b*b}} - {{4*a*c}} = {{disc}}$. Then\n$$ x = \\frac{-({{b}}) \\pm \\sqrt{ {{disc}} }}{2({{a}})} = \\frac{ {{-b}} \\pm {{radical(disc)}} }{ {{2*a}} }. $$\nSince ${{disc}}$ is not a perfect square, the roots are irrational.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "a": { "type": "int", "min": 1, "max": 3 },
          "b": { "type": "int", "min": -9, "max": 9, "exclude": [0] },
          "c": { "type": "int", "min": -9, "max": 9, "exclude": [0] },
          "disc": { "type": "expr", "expr": "b*b - 4*a*c" }
        },
        "constraints": ["disc > 0", "isint(sqrt(disc)) == 0"]
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-complete-the-square",
      "topic": "Quadratic Functions",
      "subtopic": "Vertex form",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["quadratics", "completing-the-square", "vertex"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "4",
      "source_section": "4.3",
      "statement": "Write $f(x) = x^2 {{term(b,'x')}} {{signed(c)}}$ in vertex form and state the vertex.",
      "answer": "$f(x) = (x {{signed(-h)}})^2 {{signed(k)}}$; vertex $({{h}}, {{k}})$",
      "solution": "Half of ${{b}}$ is ${{-h}}$, and $({{-h}})^2 = {{h*h}}$. So\n$$ x^2 {{term(b,'x')}} {{signed(c)}} = \\left(x^2 {{term(b,'x')}} + {{h*h}}\\right) - {{h*h}} {{signed(c)}} = (x {{signed(-h)}})^2 {{signed(k)}}. $$\nThe vertex is $({{h}}, {{k}})$.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "h": { "type": "int", "min": -7, "max": 7, "exclude": [0] },
          "k": { "type": "int", "min": -12, "max": 12, "exclude": [0] },
          "b": { "type": "expr", "expr": "-2*h" },
          "c": { "type": "expr", "expr": "h*h + k" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-factor-nonmonic",
      "topic": "Polynomials",
      "subtopic": "Factoring non-monic trinomials",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["factoring", "quadratics"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "3",
      "source_section": "3.4",
      "statement": "Factor completely: ${{coef(p*r,'x^2')}} {{term(p*s + q*r,'x')}} {{signed(q*s)}}$",
      "answer": "$({{coef(p,'x')}} {{signed(q)}})({{coef(r,'x')}} {{signed(s)}})$",
      "solution": "The product of the outer and inner terms must give the middle coefficient ${{p*s + q*r}}$ while the leading and constant terms are ${{p*r}}$ and ${{q*s}}$. Splitting accordingly gives $({{coef(p,'x')}} {{signed(q)}})({{coef(r,'x')}} {{signed(s)}})$.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "p": { "type": "int", "min": 2, "max": 4 },
          "q": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] },
          "r": { "type": "int", "min": 1, "max": 3 },
          "s": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] }
        },
        "constraints": ["gcd(p, r) == 1", "gcd(p, q) == 1", "gcd(r, s) == 1", "p*s + q*r != 0"]
      }
    },
