      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["logarithms", "expand"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "7",
      "source_section": "7.4",
      "statement": "Expand as far as possible using the properties of logarithms: $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^{ {{m}} } y}{z^{ {{n}} }}\\right)$",
      "answer": "${{m}}\\log x + \\log y - {{n}}\\log z$",
      "solution": "The quotient rule splits numerator and denominator; the product rule splits $x^{ {{m}} }y$; the power rule moves the exponents out front: ${{m}}\\log x + \\log y - {{n}}\\log z$.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "m": { "type": "int", "min": 2, "max": 6 },
          "n": { "type": "int", "min": 2, "max": 5 }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-compound-interest",
      "topic": "Exponential and Logarithmic Functions",
      "subtopic": "Exponential models",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["exponential", "word-problem", "applications"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "7",
      "source_section": "7.2",
      "statement": "An account opens with \\${{P}} and earns {{r}}\\% annual interest, compounded annually. What is the balance after {{t}} years? Round to the nearest cent.",
      "answer": "\\${{fmt(P*(1 + r/100)^t, 2)}}",
      "solution": "Use $A = P(1 + r)^t$ with $P = {{P}}$, $r = {{fmt(r/100, 2)}}$, and $t = {{t}}$:\n$$ A = {{P}}(1 {{signed(r/100)}})^{ {{t}} } = \\${{fmt(P*(1 + r/100)^t, 2)}}. $$",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "P": { "type": "choice", "values": [1000, 1500, 2000, 2500, 4000, 5000] },
          "r": { "type": "choice", "values": [3, 4, 5, 6, 8] },
          "t": { "type": "choice", "values": [5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-rational-simplify",
      "topic": "Rational Expressions",
      "subtopic": "Simplifying",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["rational-expressions", "simplify", "factoring"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "8",
      "source_section": "8.1",
      "statement": "Simplify and state any restrictions on $x$: $\\dfrac{x^2 {{term(r + s,'x')}} {{signed(r*s)}}}{x^2 {{term(r + t,'x')}} {{signed(r*t)}}}$",
      "answer": "$\\dfrac{x {{signed(s)}}}{x {{signed(t)}}}$, with $x \\ne {{-r}}$ and $x \\ne {{-t}}$",
      "solution": "Factor both: $\\dfrac{(x {{signed(r)}})(x {{signed(s)}})}{(x {{signed(r)}})(x {{signed(t)}})}$. Cancel the common factor $x {{signed(r)}}$ to get $\\dfrac{x {{signed(s)}}}{x {{signed(t)}}}$. The original denominator is zero when $x = {{-r}}$ or $x = {{-t}}$, so both are excluded.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "r": { "type": "int", "min": -7, "max": 7, "exclude": [0] },
          "s": { "type": "int", "min": -7, "max": 7, "exclude": [0] },
          "t": { "type": "int", "min": -7, "max": 7, "exclude": [0] }
        },
        "constraints": ["r != s", "r != t", "s != t"]
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-complex-arithmetic",
      "topic": "Complex Numbers",
      "subtopic": "Multiplying complex numbers",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["complex-numbers", "drill"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "4",
      "source_section": "4.8",
      "statement": "Multiply and write the result in the form $a + bi$: $({{a}} {{signed(b)}}i)({{c}} {{signed(d)}}i)$",
      "answer": "${{a*c - b*d}} {{signed(a*d + b*c)}}i$",
      "solution": "Expanding, $({{a}})({{c}}) = {{a*c}}$ and the $i^2$ term contributes $({{b}})({{d}})i^2 = {{-(b*d)}}$, so the real part is ${{a*c - b*d}}$. The imaginary parts give $({{a}})({{d}}) + ({{b}})({{c}}) = {{a*d + b*c}}$.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "a": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] },
          "b": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] },
          "c": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] },
          "d": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6, "exclude": [0] }
        },
        "constraints": ["a*d + b*c != 0"]
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-radical-equation",
      "topic": "Radical Functions",
      "subtopic": "Solving radical equations",
      "difficulty": 4,
