      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "6",
      "source_section": "6.5",
      "statement": "Solve, checking for extraneous solutions: $\\sqrt{ {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}} } = {{c}}$",
      "answer": "$x = {{frac(c*c - b, a)}}$",
      "solution": "Squaring both sides gives $ {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}} = {{c*c}} $, so $ {{coef(a,'x')}} = {{c*c - b}} $ and $x = {{frac(c*c - b, a)}}$. Since ${{c}} > 0$, squaring introduced no extraneous solution — check by substituting back.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "a": { "type": "int", "min": 1, "max": 5 },
          "b": { "type": "int", "min": -9, "max": 9, "exclude": [0] },
          "c": { "type": "int", "min": 2, "max": 8 }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-polynomial-division",
      "topic": "Polynomials",
      "subtopic": "Synthetic division",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "kind": "template",
      "tags": ["polynomials", "division", "factor-theorem"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "3",
      "source_section": "3.3",
      "statement": "Divide using synthetic division: $\\dfrac{x^3 {{term(b,'x^2')}} {{term(c,'x')}} {{signed(d)}}}{x {{signed(-r)}}}$",
      "answer": "$x^2 {{term(b + r,'x')}} {{signed(c + r*(b + r))}}$ with remainder $0$",
      "solution": "Since $x = {{r}}$ is a root, the division is exact. Bringing down the coefficients $1$, ${{b}}$, ${{c}}$, ${{d}}$ with divisor root ${{r}}$ gives quotient coefficients $1$, ${{b + r}}$, ${{c + r*(b + r)}}$ and remainder $0$.",
      "params": {
        "vars": {
          "r": { "type": "int", "min": -5, "max": 5, "exclude": [0] },
          "b": { "type": "int", "min": -6, "max": 6 },
          "c": { "type": "int", "min": -8, "max": 8 },
          "d": { "type": "expr", "expr": "-r*(c + r*(b + r))" }
        },
        "constraints": ["b + r != 0", "c + r*(b + r) != 0", "d != 0"]
      }
    },
