      "statement": "Find $f^{-1}(x)$ for $f(x) = {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}}$.",
      "answer": "$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x {{signed(-b)}}}{ {{a}} }$",
      "solution": "Write $y = {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}}$, swap $x$ and $y$, then solve: $x = {{coef(a,'y')}} {{signed(b)}}$, so $y = \\dfrac{x {{signed(-b)}}}{ {{a}} }$.",
      "params": {
