    {
      "external_key": "alg2-projectile-static",
      "topic": "Quadratic Functions",
      "subtopic": "Applications",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "kind": "static",
      "tags": ["quadratics", "word-problem", "applications", "vertex"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "4",
      "source_section": "4.4",
      "source_number": "42",
      "statement": "A ball is thrown upward from a height of 6 feet with an initial velocity of 64 feet per second, so its height after $t$ seconds is $h(t) = -16t^2 + 64t + 6$. Find the maximum height and the time at which it occurs.",
      "answer": "70 feet, at $t = 2$ seconds",
      "solution": "The vertex occurs at $t = -\\dfrac{b}{2a} = -\\dfrac{64}{2(-16)} = 2$ seconds. Then $h(2) = -16(4) + 64(2) + 6 = -64 + 128 + 6 = 70$ feet."
    },
    {
      "external_key": "alg2-piecewise-static",
      "topic": "Functions",
      "subtopic": "Piecewise functions",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "static",
      "tags": ["functions", "piecewise", "evaluate"],
      "source_book": "Course Packet",
      "source_chapter": "2",
      "source_section": "2.5",
      "source_number": "9",
      "statement": "Let\n$$ f(x) = \\begin{cases} 2x + 1 & x < 0 \\\\ x^2 & 0 \\le x < 3 \\\\ 9 & x \\ge 3 \\end{cases} $$\nEvaluate $f(-4)$, $f(0)$, $f(2)$, and $f(5)$.",
      "answer": "$f(-4) = -7$, $f(0) = 0$, $f(2) = 4$, $f(5) = 9$",
      "solution": "Each input selects a branch by which interval it falls in: $-4 < 0$ gives $2(-4) + 1 = -7$; $0 \\le 0 < 3$ gives $0^2 = 0$; $0 \\le 2 < 3$ gives $2^2 = 4$; and $5 \\ge 3$ gives $9$."
    }
